I've got this years Dilithium star.

My Valk got off to a fairly slow start. High points were BoS, a CoD
and an early magic lamp - a cure for your Grues. Bad points; no bones,
almost all shops were weapons or armour, and Odin took his own sweet
time getting me Mjolnir.
Sokoban had a BoH, and I then went down to Mine's end. I found a
sinister device and then didn't do anything with it (except lug it
around with me for the rest of the game). Next time, I'll actually try
to turn off the thing.
 I didn't get reflection until Perseus provided me with a shiny new
shield. Twice lost my mithril (and CoD, and CoI) to polytraps. On the
way back to pick up some more armour, a gremlin stole my protection and
I felt obliged to murder a shopkeeper to buy it back (from the cross
aligned minetown priest). Backdoored the castle with a RoLev and turned
the wand into SoC, GDSM, GoP, Helm of Telepathy and a failed wish for
the Sunsword (I was worried about vortexes and Grues). A spare magic
lamp later turned into a ring of free action.
Gehemmon provided as much trouble as expected to a Valk with lots of
magic markers (thank you RNG), though there were a couple of close
calls of the 'the vortex engulfs you. Your magic lamp goes out. It's
pitch dark, you might be eaten by a Grue.' type. The first amulet I saw
in the game was in Vlad's and that AoLS adorned my neck for most of the
rest of the game.
Both Rodney and Yeenogha turned up in the Sanctum, the latter kindly
dealing with the high priest for me.
No problems on the planes until fire when an Archon (with that Sunsword
I'd been wanting) read a SoCM getting... another Archon who read a SoCM
and got... a third Archon - the trend thankfully stopped there and
eventually fragmites could get back to finding the portal.
On the Astral Famine and Pesty fell to WoD, Death to Mjolnir (yep it
was the third altar). I lost the AoLS to a role character who (very
cunningly) first threw a potion of blindness of me so I couldn't see
what he was wielding, then decapitated me (I'm imagining a bullet in
the cigar case type moment). I finally got to the right altar, checked
the amulet, wielded the sinister device and ascended.
My conducts were 6 wishes, genoless, polyobjectless, no Elbereth, no
conflict. And there's now a Grue generator in the demigod's bar.

So, now to try and win the challenge, get another Dilithium star, add
to my ascended list (K,S,W,B,V so far) etc.

